ipad-keyboard-style-heading = SHORTCUT STYLE
ipad-keyboard-style-ipad = iPad
ipad-keyboard-style-herdr-prefix = Herdr prefix
ipad-keyboard-style-description = Tab labels, the status bar, and the command palette show this style. With iPad, the prefix key goes straight to the terminal and ⌘ shortcuts do the rest. With Herdr prefix, the prefix arms the chords as in the TUI; press it twice to send it to the terminal.
ipad-keyboard-prefix-key = Prefix key
ipad-keyboard-prefix-from-host = From { $host }'s Herdr config
ipad-keyboard-prefix-default = Herdr's default (no usable local prefix setting)
ipad-keyboard-prefix-local = From the local Herdr config
ipad-keyboard-prefix-edit-local = To change the leader, edit [keys].prefix in your local Herdr config. Shortcut style above changes how this app handles keys; it does not edit the leader.
ipad-keyboard-prefix-edit-path = To change the leader, edit [keys].prefix in { $path }. Shortcut style above changes how this app handles keys; it does not edit the leader.
ipad-keyboard-prefix-edit-host = To change the leader, edit [keys].prefix in { $host }'s Herdr config on that host. This app does not edit remote config files. Shortcut style above is a separate local setting.
